  "title": "Parinirvana of the Buddha at Kushinagar",
  "summary": "Buddhist tradition holds that the Buddha, in his eightieth year, fell ill after a journey from Rajagaha and died between two sala trees in the Mallas' grove near Kusinara, now Kushinagar. His death year is debated: 487-483 BC in one reckoning, 544-543 BC in Sri Lankan tradition.",
